{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 04196681b1ce81020cb669ad998f83b4fba33046 (request/merge-receipt-discharge, two commits over main 9fbc913e), primary artifact c0236ccf at internal/workroom/fold.go and its seventeen companions, under review request b6801395, governing request 1d42f753 and implementation promise b7a05e4c. No blocker: the repair is correct and well pinned, and I reproduced the reported \"idempotency key reused with different intent\" failure from the original code, so the regression tests bite. Three localized corrections belong on the live implementation commitment; this verdict does not withdraw or close it.\n\n1. The user-facing wire contract still declares the landing state the server can no longer produce. internal/app/landing.go (around line 88) now reports an empty supplied merge head as unknown with the reason \"no witnessed merge head was supplied; ancestry is unknown\" and nil ancestry booleans, and docs/reference/landing-observations.md removes the no_receipt row; but ui/src/lib/api.ts line 111 still types state as including \"no_receipt\" and ui/src/lib/spine.ts line 256 still branches on it, so that branch is dead, the case falls through to the generic \"current target ancestry is unknown\" wording, and git.reason is rendered nowhere. Fix: drop no_receipt from the union and the branch, render the reason in the unknown case, rebuild the embed (internal/service/uidist still carries the string), and publish those paths at the corrected head.\n\n2. The three recovery guards added to mergeplan.Build (internal/mergeplan/mergeplan.go about lines 1434 to 1444: TargetPairPresent coherence, and the ResolveTarget versus SealedTarget repository and ref match) have no negative control. Deleting all three in a scratch copy left ./internal/mergeplan/... and the Merge, Resume and Complete tests under ./cmd/gs/... green. The empty-acts refusal at line 1450 and the empty-shared refusal in cmd/gs/succession.go line 87 are equally unproven. The enforcing copy in gs merge (cmd/gs/main.go lines 821 to 831) is what stops a wrong destination, so this is a preview-accuracy gap, not a hole; the request's conditions still call for negative tests for mismatches and invalid receipts. Fix: one mergeplan test that plans an existing receipt whose sealed ref differs from the checkout's and asserts the target refusal, plus a case for each empty refusal.\n\n3. dischargedBy (internal/workroom/landing.go line 832) is tautological at all six call sites (fold.go 3626, 3674, 3758, 3761, 3767, 3826): every caller feeds it a receipt from mergeDeliveries.at, which already keys on the commitment's resolved repository and ref (fold.go 3879 to 3881), so a non-nil receipt already implies the destination match. Making it return true for any non-nil receipt leaves ./internal/workroom/... and ./internal/app/... green, while dropping repository and ref from the delivery key goes red. The destination rule is stated twice and only one statement is load-bearing. Fix: replace the six calls with nil checks and delete the helper, or drop the key and keep the helper; one place.\n\nSmaller notes, not required: validateMergeReceiptNow returns the retirement plan and writes mergeArtifacts through the pointer, so mergedArtifacts relies on an invariant held only by placement; the early return that skips verifySuccession on a completed retry is right (re-verifying a finished delivery against a world that moved would refuse it, which merge_completion_test sets up) but unexplained; architecture.md's layer 6 profile history stops at @22 while the @24 advance is recorded under layer 5 and on landing-observations.md, a cross-reference would help. Pre-existing and not this head: cmd/gs/main_test.go around line 5056 parses CombinedOutput as JSON, so the one-second \"verifying the durable log\" banner corrupts the parse under machine load (seen once in my parallel run, not in the serial rerun); and the recovery branch never calls RequireImplementer, unlike the fresh path, which the receipt-signer check in validateMergeReceiptNow makes low impact.\n\nArchitecture: layers 5, 6 and 7 are affected. Layer 5 changes contract: the interpreter freezes the eligible exact-head review set at receipt admission (fold.go about line 1684) and delivery no longer depends on retirement-plan membership, advancing the projection profile to workroom-fold@24; the head's architecture.md candidate 7de044db and the landing-observations.md candidate record that correctly and old caches are rebuilt. Layer 6 keeps its witness field shape (landing_receipt and approved_not_landed keep their meanings) and is now destination-matched, which the page records. Layer 7 changes behaviour, not shape: recovery appends only the missing canonical acts and merge-plan gains a complete mode, documented on gs/merge.md, gs/merge-plan.md and mcp/merge_plan.md. The architecture-adjacent miss is outside the artifact set: the UI wire type in item 1.\n\nSecurity: the trust boundaries hold. Retirement authority and delivery are now separate and the authority half is unchanged: validateMergeReceiptNow still requires an effective ratified exact-candidate approval, an independent implementer, a receipt signed by that implementer and the temporal world rule, and the frozen set is a strict subset of the artifacts the approval itself cites, so a receipt cannot reach anything the reviewer did not sign; the new TestMergeDischargeKeepsReceiptAuthorityGuards covers those negatives. Destination is part of delivery identity, so a later receipt into another ref can neither hide nor forge closure; dropping repository and ref from the delivery key goes red. PendingSuccession is a completion filter and not a new authority or idempotency rule: it matches only effective acts by the merger's own fingerprint over signed content and ordered citations, ignoring only admission's automatic staleness testimony; dropping the actor filter, the citation prepend, the label resolution or either staleness exemption goes red; a retired receipt and an ambiguous match refuse; missing acts keep their deterministic keys and pass ordinary admission; a complete retry appends nothing after staleness moves; a partial suffix resumes. The one new guard without a red proof is item 2; the enforcing copy in gs merge stands. I found no way for an unapproved head, a wrong target or a foreign actor to discharge a commitment. This is assigned repair under #21944, not a self-initiated delivery.\n\nSimplification: item 3 (one destination rule, not two), plus the two smaller notes above. No further cut without weakening the conditions.\n\nChecks executed at 04196681 in a fresh detached worktree under my session, bash pipefail: go build ./... rc 0; go vet ./... rc 0; go test -count=1 over internal/workroom (ok 6.9 s), internal/mergeplan (ok 4.3 s), internal/app (ok 67.2 s) and cmd/gs (one failure on the first pass, TestBatchProcessReadsItsFileAndReportsFailures/positional_file, the pre-existing banner-in-CombinedOutput race under parallel load; serial rerun of ./cmd/gs/... ok in 383.5 s); go test -race over workroom and mergeplan rc 0; go test ./internal/docset/... rc 0 (123.4 s); git diff --check rc 0. Fourteen guard mutants applied one at a time in a scratch copy outside the repository: twelve killed by named tests (retirement-plan membership, delivery key, ambiguous match, retired receipt, no_receipt restoration, both staleness exemptions, label resolution, citation prepend, actor filter, complete reporting, whole-suffix append), two survived (the Build target guards, item 2; the tautological dischargedBy, item 3). The primary artifact's evidence claims check out: 13 source and test files at a6c7b6f5 and exactly five docs at the head; five corrected cache-profile expectations plus one added negative; @24 rejects prior caches; four original-code overlays reproduced; vet and build stated as carried and re-run by me at the head. All twenty-four cited artifacts are live and not stale. Publish the corrected exact head citing this finding and request fresh independent review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c0236ccf0c1cf6dcbfd80131394190a80c86ccae","binding":"assigned","head":"04196681b1ce81020cb669ad998f83b4fba33046","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f45b0ba0a00a5f7be239757a5ab80d8aec9b387a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f305ddf7e0713bff662d6ed2517f45ceb7a05e4c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:091194db91097175ef18c2cdceffc2d92ab170e0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}